module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.MvPolynomial.Cardinal
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.FormallyEtaleScheme
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.FormallySmooth.UnramifiedChartCriterion

/-!
# Formal étaleness read off from étale scheme charts

Let `ψ` be a morphism of the big fppf site over a scheme `S`. This file compares formal
étaleness of the induced transformation `yoneda.map ψ` of representable presheaves, which
tests lifting problems only against square-zero closed immersions of *objects of the site*,
with formal étaleness of the underlying morphism of schemes, which tests them against all
first-order thickenings of affine schemes.

The two agree. One direction is immediate, since a lifting problem for the site is in
particular one for schemes. The other is the content of the file: a thickening of affine
schemes which the site need not contain is replaced by one it does contain, of bounded
cardinality, over which the same problem is solvable, and the solutions over the members of
an affine open cover of the thickened scheme are glued.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.formallyEtale_yonedaMap_of_schemeFormallyEtale`: a morphism of the
  site whose underlying morphism of schemes is formally étale induces a formally étale
  transformation of representable presheaves.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_lift_of_formallyEtale_yonedaMap_of_contains`: the lifting
  property of `yoneda.map ψ` restated for a first-order thickening of affine schemes *which
  the site contains*.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_lift_of_formallyEtale_yonedaMap_of_isAffine`: the lifting
  property for an arbitrary first-order thickening of affine schemes, when `ψ` is a morphism
  of affine objects of the site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.formallyEtale_resLE_of_formallyEtale_yonedaMap`: the restriction of
  the morphism of schemes to an affine open of the source over an affine open of the target is
  formally étale.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.schemeFormallyEtale_of_formallyEtale_yonedaMap`: the morphism of
  schemes underlying `ψ` is formally étale.

## Implementation notes

Uniqueness of lifts is not the issue: it comes from
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.schemeFormallyUnramified_of_formallyEtale_yonedaMap`, which reads it
off the Tag 04G8 criterion for formal unramifiedness. The issue is existence, and it is solved
in three steps.

*Bounded size.* A lifting problem for an affine `ψ` against a first-order thickening
`Spec A' ⟶ Spec A` is a square of rings. Replacing `A'` by the subring generated by the image
of `Γ(Y, ⊤)` together with one chosen preimage of each element of `Γ(X, ⊤)`, and `A` by the
image of that subring, gives a square-zero surjection of rings of cardinality at most
`max ℵ₀ (max #Γ(X, ⊤) #Γ(Y, ⊤))`. Both section rings are at most the size of the respective
object of the site by `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.mk_sections_le_size`, so the two spectra lie
below the cutoff and the site contains them; the original problem factors through the small
one, so a solution there solves it. This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.boundedSquareZeroPresentation`.

*Affine opens.* An affine open `V` of the source over an affine open `U` of the target is
again an object of the site, because an open immersion is a monomorphism locally of finite
presentation and so does not increase size
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.size_le_of_mono_locallyOfFinitePresentation`). The two inclusions
are étale charts, so Tag 04G5 and Tag 049T transport formal étaleness of `yoneda.map ψ` to the
restricted morphism of the site, and the previous step applies to it.

*Gluing.* With formal étaleness available on all affine charts, each point of the thickened
scheme has an affine open neighbourhood over which the lifting problem is solvable — the
argument of `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_isAffineOpen_lift_of_unramified_flat`, with the
flatness-and-unramifiedness input replaced by the previous step. The local solutions agree on
overlaps by `Stacks.Smooth.lift_unique` and glue by
`Stacks.Smooth.exists_lift_of_isOpenCover`.

